menu "figma2lvgl example"

    config EXAMPLE_TOUCH_PIN_CS
        int "XPT2046 touch chip-select GPIO"
        range 0 48
        default 1 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32C3
        default 25
        help
            GPIO for the XPT2046 touch controller's chip-select. Touch shares
            the display's SPI bus (host, clock, MOSI and MISO from the
            ILI9486 driver settings), so only its chip-select is set here.
            On ESP32-C3 boards avoid GPIO8 (onboard LED and strapping pin),
            GPIO9 (BOOT strapping pin) and GPIO2 (strapping pin).

    config EXAMPLE_TOUCH_MIRROR_X
        bool "Mirror touch X"
        default y
        help
            Flip the touch X axis so taps land where they are drawn. Where
            the XPT2046's origin sits depends on how the module wires its
            resistive film, not on the display settings. The default fits
            the common red 3.5" ILI9486 + XPT2046 module with
            esp-lcd-ili9486 2.x, whose touch origin is at the corner
            opposite the display's. If a tap on the left of the screen hits
            a widget on the right, toggle this.

    config EXAMPLE_TOUCH_MIRROR_Y
        bool "Mirror touch Y"
        default y
        help
            Flip the touch Y axis. As for X: toggle this if a tap near the
            top hits a widget near the bottom.

endmenu
